      "number": 1,
      "id": "I_kwDOONqcxc8AAAABEs8Uxw",
      "title": "Editorial: missing reference, nonstandard terminology, hard-coded example number",
      "url": "https://github.com/json-structure/import/issues/1",
      "state": "CLOSED",
      "author": "clemensv",
      "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "The following minor editorial issues were found during review:\n\n### 1. Missing RFC6901 in normative references\n\nThe draft discusses JSON Pointer semantics but `RFC6901` is not listed in the normative references metadata block.\n\n### 2. Nonstandard term \"jsonpointer instance\"\n\nThe text refers to \"any `jsonpointer` instance (`` or `` or ``)\" \u2014 this should use the standard term \"JSON Pointer reference\" with a citation to RFC 6901.\n\n### 3. Hard-coded \"Example 4.1\" reference\n\nThe text says \"The external schema remains the same as in Example 4.1.\" \u2014 this should use an internal cross-reference anchor (e.g., `{{example-import-external-schema}}`) to avoid breakage if examples are reordered.",
      "createdAt": "2026-06-08T06:27:39Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-06-08T08:53:21Z",
      "closedAt": "2026-06-08T08:53:21Z",
      "comments": []
    }
  ],
